105
00:07:28,867 --> 00:07:35,562
Suppose a gateway reserves an operation
key, calls an external service, and

106
00:07:35,562 --> 00:07:37,854
then stores the returned receipt.

107
00:07:39,146 --> 00:07:47,014
A crash after the external commit, but
before the receipt write leaves an intent

108
00:07:47,018 --> 00:07:49,552
record with no completion evidence.

109
00:07:50,518 --> 00:07:56,941
Reserving first can stop a second worker
from immediately doing the same work, but

110
00:07:56,941 --> 00:07:59,332
it can leave the operation unresolved.

111
00:08:00,377 --> 00:08:03,830
Writing only afterward
creates the opposite risk.

112
00:08:04,368 --> 00:08:08,973
A crash can leave no local record, even
