it before stopping a completion receipt.

241
00:18:15,483 --> 00:18:19,536
The provider offered lookups
and documented idempotency

242
00:18:19,542 --> 00:18:21,213
contract for that operation.

243
00:18:21,773 --> 00:18:23,346
Which next step would you choose?

244
00:18:23,744 --> 00:18:29,429
A fresh key, a failure response, or
recovery using the original reference?

245
00:18:30,429 --> 00:18:35,049
Use the original operation reference
to investigate or retry with

246
00:18:35,049 --> 00:18:39,368
the same provider key when the
documented contract permits it.

247
00:18:39,858 --> 00:18:43,449
A fresh key could create
an unrelated second order.

248
00:18:44,442 --> 00:18:49,070
A failure response would claim
knowledge we do not h- yet have.

249
00:18:49,934 --> 00:18:52,766
Lookup still needs the
appropriate read permission.

250
00:18:53,391 --> 00:18:57,249
If the recovery call might
execute the operation, check its

251
00:18:57,249 --> 00:18:58,907
current execution authority too.

252
00:19:00,147 --> 00:19:04,953
The provider contract determines what
evidence and behavior we can safely expect

253
00:19:05,953 --> 00:19:11,518
A read-only lookup and an idempotent retry
can have different authority requirements.

254
00:19:12,079 --> 00:19:16,927
The latter may still execute an operation
that never reached the provider.

255
00:19:17,879 --> 00:19:21,701
Choose the recovery call
accordingly to both its effect

256
00:19:21,720 --> 00:19:23,867
semantics and the current policy

257
00:19:24,867 --> 00:19:28,092
Now remove both provider capabilities.

258
00:19:28,630 --> 00:19:33,313
There is no lookup by operation and
no safe same key retry contract.

259
00:19:33,816 --> 00:19:34,783
What changes?

260
00:19:36,686 --> 00:19:41,147
The absence of a local receipt
still cannot establish that the

261
00:19:41,179 --> 00:19:45,920
order never happened, but the
easy recovery path has gone.

262
00:19:46,554 --> 00:19:50,651
Preserve the unresolved state
and give an operator the original

263
00:19:50,651 --> 00:19:54,874
identifiers, dispatch evidence,
and next investigation step.

264
00:19:55,703 --> 00:19:59,845
A deliberate second operation can be
a business decision if the remaining

265
00:19:59,845 --> 00:20:01,436
duplication risk is understood.

266
00:20:02,112 --> 00:20:06,006
It must not arise silently
from a generic timeout handler.

267
00:20:06,635 --> 00:20:09,102
This is the operational
meaning of unknown.

268
00:20:10,204 --> 00:20:16,454
The system knows why evidence is missing,
who owns the investigation, and which

269
00:20:16,462 --> 00:20:18,585
fresh mutations remain constrained

270
00:20:19,585 --> 00:20:23,937
Choose one mutating tool and
one effect you can observe

271
00:20:24,328 --> 00:20:25,883
in a controlled environment.

272
00:20:26,504 --> 00:20:31,074
Pick an effect with an oracle you can
inspect safely in a test environment.

273
00:20:32,453 --> 00:20:37,063
Write down the promise about repeat
calls and the period for which it holds.

274
00:20:37,797 --> 00:20:42,485
Run the clean path, then
the after-commit reply loss.

275
00:20:43,058 --> 00:20:47,096
Add a worker restart and a
stale worker case only when the

276
00:20:47,096 --> 00:20:49,094
basic harness is trustworthy.

277
00:20:49,780 --> 00:20:54,299
Evaluate both the downstream effect
and the caller-visible recovery state.

278
00:20:54,861 --> 00:20:59,057
If the provider cannot support
safe resolution, a truthful

279
00:20:59,118 --> 00:21:03,142
unresolved result is a successful
assertion of the limitation.

280
00:21:04,118 --> 00:21:09,745
Even though the integration may
need further work before autonomous

281
00:21:09,968 --> 00:21:15,031
use, the test should expose exactly
which promise the system cannot keep

282
00:21:16,031 --> 00:21:20,733
Retain the injected fault location,
operation key, effect evidence, and

283
00:21:20,733 --> 00:21:22,417
the final caller status together.

284
00:21:23,414 --> 00:21:26,626
Another engineer should be able
to explain the result from that

285
00:21:26,660 --> 00:21:31,037
evidence without relying on a
successful lookup chat transcript

286
00:21:32,037 --> 00:21:33,632
Return to the opening order.

287
00:21:34,152 --> 00:21:37,475
The timeout tells us that
the caller lacks a response.

288
00:21:37,671 --> 00:21:40,265
It does not tell us that
the service lacks an order.

289
00:21:40,846 --> 00:21:45,683
A safe recovery path keeps the logical
operation stable, checks the effect

290
00:21:45,730 --> 00:21:51,137
boundary, and returns the strongest
truthful outcome supported by evidence.

291
00:21:51,805 --> 00:21:56,431
When the evidence is incomplete,
unknown is a valid state with

292
00:21:56,431 --> 00:21:58,066
a constrained next action.

293
00:21:59,087 --> 00:22:02,855
The public repository gives
you a small baseline and a

294
00:22:02,855 --> 00:22:04,411
positive control to inspect.

295
00:22:04,914 --> 00:22:08,452
The larger matrix gives you
the next experiments to run

296
00:22:08,780 --> 00:22:10,220
against your own contract.

297
00:22:10,826 --> 00:22:15,098
If you leave with one change for
tomorrow, make the retry policy

298
00:22:15,147 --> 00:22:19,895
for mutating tool answer what
evidence permits another effect.

299
00:22:20,377 --> 00:22:20,924
Thank you.
